# Patient completion page configuration (Vite). Non-secret build/runtime vars only.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) or set in your shell / hosting env.
#
# Base URL of the Medplum server. The patient client is unauthenticated and
# credential-free (ADR-0010 A3) - it never signs in - but `MedplumProvider`
# still needs a base URL to construct its client.
# Defaults to the local docker-compose Medplum when unset.
VITE_MEDPLUM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8103/

# Same-origin path of the Access-link publicWebhook Bot - the single
# unauthenticated touchpoint for open + submit (ADR-0005). Medplum sends no CORS
# headers on /webhook, so the app calls it same-origin and the dev server (or a
# prod reverse proxy) routes /webhook to Medplum - see vite.config.ts.
# `npm run medplum:deploy-bots` writes this to `.env.local`. Example shape:
# VITE_ACCESS_LINK_WEBHOOK_URL=/webhook/<project-membership-id>

# Set to "true" to build the public-demo variant, which carries the persistent
# "Public demo - synthetic data only" banner on every screen (ADR-0012). The
# hosted deploy sets it; leave it unset locally so `dev:full` is banner-free.
# VITE_DEMO_BANNER=true
